# playpick cell: mode=raid boss=crowns spec=paladin:holy style=good size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=390x844,touch save=fresh.
#
# boss=crowns in mode=raid is not a coverage label -- direction.md's #7 thread
# (2026-09-27-3.play and others) already confirmed the direct invite-hash
# pulls this exact fight, The Three Crowns. That thread's whole finding is
# that toward-boss styles (melee/good/idle) beeline at whatever body
# hud().boss currently names, which is sometimes the untouchable decoy, and
# park the whole fight parked in its thirst radius instead of the real crown
# -- but every `good` pull on record so far (warrior:protection normal,
# paladin:retribution heroic, both 2026-09-26/27) was a damage spec walking
# onto a damage target. This is the first `good`-style *healer* against this
# fight: paladin:holy's `good` steering presumably targets the lowest-hp
# living ally to heal rather than a boss-faction body to hit, so the question
# this asks that no dps pull could: does a healer's `good` command even walk
# toward hud().boss at all, or does it stay near the raid instead and dodge
# the decoy trap by accident, the same way `dodge`'s style already does for a
# different reason (no toward-boss term at all).
open #b=crowns&s=25&h=1
targets
tap class:paladin:holy
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

play good 90
bill
state
shot mid1

play good 90
bill
state
shot mid2

play good 90
bill
state
shot mid3

play good 60
bill
says
state
shot end
